;; The world seat: plays the outside world an org's brief implies, one
;; simulated day per firing, for seven days. It only ever sits on a
;; clone (docs/spec-demo-clones.md): its rows are the week the film
;; shows before the person merges the org. Epic cafa6106, M3c.
{:template
 {:params {:brief "The org_plan's brief, the one paragraph the person typed: what this business is and does."
           :kinds "The org's kinds whose create doors the outside world knocks on, by name, comma-separated: every kind whose create door a non-staff cast member's :scope holds in the seed (the request a customer files, the record a supplier sends, the payment a payer makes). Scope and :delivers get one create entry per kind. A seed that still gives :kind alone fills it as a one-element :kinds."
           :cast "The ids of the cast members the world plays, as the seed's :cast gives them, comma-separated: the customers, suppliers and callers whose words the rows carry. Never the org's own people."
           :day_one "The date day 1 is, as the clone's seed resolves [:days 0] (YYYY-MM-DD). Day k is day_one plus k-1 days."
           :domain_id "The id of the org's domain row: the seat's :domain ref."}
  :lists [:kinds]
  :aliases {:kind :kinds}
  :note "Seat this only in a clone's seed, never in an org that is live: it writes rows a real customer did not file. Seven firings make the week; an eighth finds day 7 already written and does nothing."}
 :seat
 {:name "world"
  :mode "fired"
  :rows_per_firing 1
  :cadence_seconds 3600
  :fire_interval_seconds 300
  :max_open_sittings 1
  :standing_ttl_seconds 604800
  :budget_usd_per_week 5M
  :sitting_budget_tokens 80000
  :sitting_idle_seconds 1800
  :keep_transcripts "fired"
  :transcript_days 30
  :acts_as_cast true
  :domain "{{domain_id}}"
  :charter "You play the outside world for one business across seven simulated days. The business: {{brief}} Each firing is one day. Find it: read the rows you created of the kinds {{kinds}}; the next day is one past the latest day they carry, day 1 on {{day_one}}, day k on {{day_one}} plus k-1 days; after day 7, do nothing. Write that day's 1 to 3 rows across those kinds, each through its kind's create door, in the words of one cast member ({{cast}}) and made as that member, with day k's date as today. The week has an arc: on day 2 something goes wrong that the brief implies (a record is late, a request is too thin, a payer disputes); on day 5 the outside world answers the house's chase or escalation; on day 7 it brings what finishes a job (the last record, a payment). Other days stay ordinary. A refusal is part of the week the film shows, not an error: never retry it to make it pass, never change a row after you create it, and never take a door the org's own seats hold; they answer."
  :instructions "You sit in `world`. For your one day: list the rows you created of each kind in {{kinds}} (waymark_query with that kind, return \"summary\") to find the day. Then create that day's 1 to 3 rows with waymark_invoke, kind one of {{kinds}}, action \"create\", no id, and `as` the id of the cast member whose words it carries. When a create refuses, leave it: that refusal is the day's event. When halted or parked, say why and stop. When the Stop hook asks you to close the sitting, make that one call; the note names the day and each row you created or that refused."
  :scope [{:kind "{{kinds}}" :actions ["create"]}]
  :delivers [{:kind "{{kinds}}" :action "create"}]}}
